The model has 20 real-valued flux symbols, including a dedicated objReaction, and 12 exact mass-balance rows spanning 1 to 9 reactions. Row widths and stoichiometric coefficients are scaled empirical samples from the canonical E. coli model. Ordinary reactions are boxed at the selected numeric flux scale; one exchange reaction has a narrow positive interval, while objReaction is linked through the stoichiometric system rather than explicitly boxed.

Objective regime: boundary. The dedicated objective uses the E. coli family-native assertion direction `(>= threshold objReaction)` and is set to the minimum feasible upper threshold (satisfiable).
Numeric profile: native. Flux bounds use 1000, and row coefficients are sampled from the canonical family model.

This file is a structural floating-point translation of that source instance. Real variables are replaced by (_ FloatingPoint 15 113) variables. Real arithmetic is replaced by roundNearestTiesToEven floating-point arithmetic, and numeric constants are pre-rounded once to exact target-format literals. Linear comparisons become floating-point comparisons; equality uses IEEE fp.eq. No finite-value guards are added.

Floating point is not the reals; satisfiability is not assumed to survive this translation. The translated status is unknown.

